Subject: [PATCH] Track fixed-capacity request steering controls in V2 state

Replay baseline: r6x author head 7316c7f9fae1bc4a0b7ab1848de0db4143eec5d2 and preceding
0500-series downstream patches. The original base and validation entries
below are historical provenance; r6x qualification is recorded separately.

Base: r6v plus request steering contracts. Rationale: lifecycle-owned slots and GPU expansion from final verification offsets, without per-step host copies or scale banks. Quality: dummy/padding rows are stock and cancellation clears reused slots. Validation: CPU ragged rows, CED/SP reference layout and lifecycle tests; GPU row checks are in the next patch. Upstream status: independent downstream experiment; no upstream submission.
